1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:09,948
Welcome to CarbonProof AI, an evidence-first environmental verification platform engineered to restore cryptographic integrity to voluntary carbon markets.

2
00:00:09,898 --> 00:00:14,796
We begin by authenticating into the platform using the administrator role.

3
00:00:14,796 --> 00:00:27,258
On the main dashboard, market operators and auditors have immediate visibility into aggregate system metrics: total active projects, verified carbon credits, and dual-layer settlement indicators.

4
00:00:27,258 --> 00:00:31,135
Every metric is backed by verified data records.

5
00:00:31,135 --> 00:00:37,334
Next, we register a new environmental carbon project through the platform's intake interface.

6
00:00:37,334 --> 00:00:48,138
We enter the project details: the Mount Kenya Native Reforestation and Agroforestry Project, adopting the verified VM0007 methodology.

7
00:00:48,138 --> 00:00:55,408
We specify the host region in Kenya's Central Highlands, register the external registry reference, and submit.

8
00:00:55,408 --> 00:01:02,921
The project is created through our REST API and initialized in draft status, ready for primary evidence intake.

9
00:01:02,921 --> 00:01:11,135
In CarbonProof AI, carbon claims are treated as unverified hypotheses until backed by immutable evidence documents.

10
00:01:11,135 --> 00:01:16,849
We now upload actual project documentation directly to the project's evidence vault.

11
00:01:16,849 --> 00:01:24,847
First, we attach the Project Design Document, a comprehensive PDF detailing baseline additionality barriers.

12
00:01:24,847 --> 00:01:34,426
Next, we upload field biomass sample inventory data in CSV format, recording tree diameter and allometric carbon calculations.

13
00:01:34,426 --> 00:01:43,508
Finally, we attach satellite remote sensing telemetry in JSON format, capturing canopy height models and vegetation indices.

14
00:01:43,508 --> 00:01:48,533
Each document is validated, securely persisted, and indexed.

15
00:01:48,533 --> 00:01:54,145
Every uploaded file is immediately fingerprinted using SHA-256.

16
00:01:54,145 --> 00:02:05,434
Notice our ethical verification boundary: matching cryptographic fingerprints guarantees that stored bytes are byte-for-byte identical to what was submitted, preventing retro-active alteration.

17
00:02:05,434 --> 00:02:16,454
We trigger the platform's integrity verification action: the backend reads the stored file, recalculates the cryptographic digest, and confirms an exact match against the ledger.

18
00:02:16,454 --> 00:02:22,321
It establishes immutable custody without claiming to replace on-ground physical inspection.

19
00:02:22,321 --> 00:02:28,406
With primary evidence in custody, we execute the platform's deterministic rules engine.

20
00:02:28,406 --> 00:02:39,337
Unlike opaque black-box neural networks, CarbonProof evaluates submitted projects against standardized carbon accounting criteria using transparent, reproducible rules.

21
00:02:39,337 --> 00:02:51,977
The engine evaluates additionality hurdles, baseline deforestation credibility, boundary validation, and provenance attachment, generating an overall risk score and an itemized breakdown.

22
00:02:51,977 --> 00:02:56,888
Reviewers can inspect each individual finding produced by the rules engine.

23
00:02:56,888 --> 00:03:07,232
Here, the system flags the absence of registered land tenure deed attachments, assigning a moderate severity and recommending submission of official cadastral records.

24
00:03:07,232 --> 00:03:16,378
The rules engine provides clear, actionable remediation guidance so project proponents know exactly what evidentiary gaps must be resolved.

25
00:03:16,378 --> 00:03:19,452
Integrity requires strict governance.

26
00:03:19,452 --> 00:03:24,094
We switch to the reviewer account to demonstrate separation of duties.

27
00:03:24,094 --> 00:03:31,556
Under our platform's governance model, project developers are prohibited from reviewing or approving their own submissions.

28
00:03:31,556 --> 00:03:45,791
An accredited reviewer audits the evidence vault and risk findings, records written justifications detailing the additionality verification, and submits an official approval decision, transitioning the project to verified internal status.

29
00:03:45,791 --> 00:03:57,526
Once verified, the platform authorizes the creation and issuance of credit batches, protected by mandatory idempotency keys to eliminate duplicate minting across network retries.

30
00:03:57,526 --> 00:04:02,143
We mint five thousand metric tons of verified carbon credits.

31
00:04:02,143 --> 00:04:10,306
Next, we retire two hundred and fifty credits on behalf of a named corporate beneficiary for Scope 3 voluntary offsetting.

32
00:04:10,306 --> 00:04:19,949
The transaction settles directly against our Solidity smart contract on the EVM node, burning the credits and returning an immutable on-chain transaction receipt.

33
00:04:20,140 --> 00:04:23,980
Transparency extends to all market participants.

34
00:04:23,930 --> 00:04:32,642
In an unauthenticated session, any corporate buyer, auditor, or regulator can access the Zero-Trust Public Verification Portal.

35
00:04:32,642 --> 00:04:45,984
By querying the project identifier or evidence hash, the portal retrieves public project status, verified evidence fingerprints, and retirement certificate serials without exposing confidential operational data.

36
00:04:45,984 --> 00:04:57,540
Finally, our immutable Audit Trail logs every state transition, evidence verification, reviewer approval, and settlement event with cryptographic timestamps and actor attribution.

37
00:04:57,540 --> 00:05:07,680
CarbonProof AI delivers deterministic rigor and cryptographic certainty, transforming voluntary carbon markets into a verifiable, trustworthy ecosystem.
